 "About Adjudix": "/about",
 "Why ADR-i": "/about",
 "Adjudix exists because the choice of forum shouldn't be an afterthought. Institutional alternative dispute resolution replaces an uncertain, case-by-case negotiation over process with the published, predictable Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0} — known to both sides before a dispute ever arises. Our unique, hybrid approach covers both the resolution of a dispute and its implementation, globally.": "/about",
 "Our founding rationale": "/about",
 "Most disputes in India are resolved one of two ways: through the courts, on a timeline and under rules designed for every kind of case rather than any one kind, or through ad hoc arbitration or mediation, where the parties negotiate procedure from a blank page every time a disagreement arises. Adjudix was founded to offer a third option: a standing institution with the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure, {0}, a panel of vetted specialists organized by dispute type, and a Training Institute that gives the next generation of arbitrators, conciliators, and mediators a defined path into the profession.": "/about",
 "That combination — resolution, training, and membership, under one roof — is deliberate. An institution that only convenes panels has no pipeline of new practitioners; one that only trains has nowhere for graduates to practice. Adjudix treats dispute resolution, education, and professional standing as one continuous system rather than three separate businesses.": "/about",
 "What sets Adjudix apart": "/about",
 "Hybrid model of dispute resolution": "/about",
 "Our flagship: mediation first, converting to a binding award only if it's needed.": "/about",
 "Global implementation": "/about",
 "Awards, settlements, and orders carried through to implementation, in India and worldwide.": "/about",
 "Corporate resolution": "/about",
 "Standing dispute resolution for businesses, without disrupting the relationship.": "/about",
 "Emergency arbitration": "/about",
 "Urgent interim relief before a full tribunal is constituted.": "/about",
 "Contract & clause drafting": "/about",
 "Contracts and arbitration clauses drafted to hold up when a dispute arises.": "/about",
 "Trainings": "/about",
 "Six certification tracks for professionals and students.": "/about",
 "Institutional ADR vs. ad hoc or litigation": "/about",
 "The difference isn't philosophical — it shows up in exactly how a dispute gets decided.": "/about",
